WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.200
SmartVest Investing Academy.

2
00:00:03.150 --> 00:00:06.400
Lesson 7: What is Compounding?

3
00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:12.725
Albert Einstein is often said to have called compound interest the eighth wonder of the world.

4
00:00:12.725 --> 00:00:17.250
But what is it mathematically, and why does it matter to you?

5
00:00:17.250 --> 00:00:22.300
Simple growth means earning returns only on your original principal.

6
00:00:22.300 --> 00:00:29.425
Compounding means earning returns on your principal PLUS all the accumulated returns from previous years.

7
00:00:29.425 --> 00:00:33.413
Think of it like a snowball rolling down a snowy hill.

8
00:00:33.413 --> 00:00:36.375
At first, it grows slowly.

9
00:00:36.375 --> 00:00:43.462
But as it rolls further, its larger surface area picks up even more snow on every rotation.

10
00:00:43.462 --> 00:00:49.725
Imagine you invest ₹1,00,000 at a hypothetical return of 10% per year.

11
00:00:49.725 --> 00:00:56.475
In Year 1, you earn ₹10,000, bringing your total to ₹1,10,000.

12
00:00:56.475 --> 00:01:05.450
In Year 2, you earn 10% not on ₹1,00,000, but on ₹1,10,000—which is ₹11,000.

13
00:01:05.450 --> 00:01:11.088
By Year 10, your money grows to over ₹2.59 Lakhs.

14
00:01:11.088 --> 00:01:19.675
By Year 20, it reaches approximately ₹6.72 Lakhs—without adding a single extra rupee!

15
00:01:19.675 --> 00:01:26.275
The most critical ingredient in compounding is not how much money you start with—it is TIME.

16
00:01:26.275 --> 00:01:31.488
The earlier you start, the more powerful the compounding snowball becomes.

17
00:01:31.487 --> 00:01:34.537
SmartVest Investing Academy.

18
00:01:34.537 --> 00:01:36.362
Learn first.

19
00:01:36.362 --> 00:01:38.812
Invest with understanding.
